---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT, POLICY_DATE } from "../consts";
---

<Base title="Terms" description="Terms of use for dynshift.com.">
  <section class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="muted small">Last updated {POLICY_DATE}.</p>

    <h2>This site</h2>
    <p>
      dynshift.com is DynShift's studio site. By using it you agree to these
      terms. If you do not agree, please do not use it.
    </p>

    <h2>The software it links to</h2>
    <p>
      Each project is governed by its own licence, not by this page: products
      under the GNU GPL-3.0, libraries under the MIT licence, as stated in each
      repository. Those licences, and each product site's own terms, decide
      what you may do with the software.
    </p>

    <h2>Content</h2>
    <p>
      The site's design, logo, writing and images belong to DynShift and are
      not licensed for reuse, except where a page says otherwise. DynShift and
      PhonePad are unregistered trademarks of DynShift. Other names (Xbox,
      Windows, Flutter, React) belong to their owners and are used only to say
      what a tool works with.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising and links</h2>
    <p>
      Some pages carry advertising supplied by Google, labelled
      <em>Advertisement</em>. DynShift does not choose individual ads or endorse
      what they offer. Links to other sites are provided for convenience;
      those sites are not DynShift's responsibility.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The site is provided as it is. It is kept accurate, but it may be wrong
      or out of date, and nothing on it is a guarantee. To the extent the law
      allows, DynShift is not liable for any loss arising from using the site.
      Nothing here limits rights you have that cannot be limited by law.
    </p>

    <h2>Law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of India. If you are a consumer, you
      also keep the protection of the mandatory laws of the country you live in.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      When these terms change, the date above changes. Questions:
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  section {
    padding-block: clamp(24px, 5vw, 56px);
  }
</style>
